-<ul class="pts">
-  <li><b>Fill carries exposure.</b> Solid is the whole value; an outline is none of it. Nothing about the spectrum depends on colour, so it survives a monochrome export and a reader who cannot distinguish hues.</li>
-  <li><b>Tokenized is an outline with a centre.</b> No value reaches the agent, but something persists: the same input always produces the same token. The dot is that persistence.</li>
-  <li><b>Aggregate is three marks, not one.</b> The value exists only as part of a group, and the mark says so.</li>
-  <li><b>Undecided is the only dashed mark and the only yellow one.</b> It is not a sixth treatment: it is work waiting. Yellow already means “needs your decision” in this console, and it sits behind an ink outline rather than carrying the line.</li>
-  <li><b>Withheld is grey, undecided is yellow.</b> Both show nothing to an agent and they are entirely different situations. One is a decision; the other is its absence.</li>
-</ul>
