-<h2>Which way a change goes</h2>
-<p class="note">The console's existing audit convention has the right instinct: in a governance product the risky act is the permissive one. This makes it a visual rule rather than a colour choice in one screen.</p>
-<div class="dirs">
-  <div class="dir open">
-    <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="10.5" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M13 18V8m0 0l-4 4m4-4l4 4" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
-    <h3>Exposing</h3>
-    <p>More reaches an agent than before. Reversible as configuration, not in consequence: once a value has been read, it has been read, and a record says so.</p>
-  </div>
-  <div class="dir shut">
-    <svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="13" cy="13" r="10.5" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M13 8v10m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
-    <h3>Restricting</h3>
-    <p>Less reaches an agent than before. Answers already given are unchanged; future ones carry less.</p>
-  </div>
