-<h2>What this is not</h2>
-<ul class="pts">
-  <li><b>Not decoration.</b> Every mark carries one fact that is otherwise only in text. Anything that adds no information does not earn a place, because a screen where everything is decorated has nothing that stands out.</li>
-  <li><b>Not a colour system.</b> The spectrum reads in monochrome. Background fills distinguish undecided from decided; ink arrows distinguish exposing from restricting.</li>
-  <li><b>Not new tokens.</b> Everything here is drawn with <code>--plum</code>, <code>--ink-2</code>, <code>--ink-3</code>, <code>--ink</code>, <code>--yellow-bg</code>, <code>--green-bg</code> and <code>--green-dk</code>. The values on this page are the real tokens from <code>docs/opintel-master.css</code>.</li>
-</ul>
-
-<p class="foot">A proposal, not an implementation. If the marks are right, they become a small set of inline SVGs in the master stylesheet's existing badge and row patterns, used everywhere a treatment, a state, an object or a direction appears — the entitlements tree, the schema explorer, evidence records, suggestions, the dashboard feed and the agent twin.</p>
