-<section><h2>Released under custody — item 5.36</h2><p>The seventh treatment is a disc containing a closed padlock. Place custody between tokenized and withheld on the exposure spectrum. It uses the existing plum token, which no other treatment uses. Row and list marks use plum; exposure fills and their legend marks also use plum, with the uniform ink outline shared by all legend marks. No new colour is introduced. Plum contrasts 19.07:1 against the white card and 17.77:1 against surface-2; the white padlock on a plum legend disc has the same 19.07:1 contrast. The mark means sealed delivery requiring redemption, never recall.</p><svg width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 34 34" role="img" aria-label="Released under custody"><circle cx="17" cy="17" r="12" fill="none" stroke="var(--plum)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M13 16v-3a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3" fill="none" stroke="var(--plum)" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="11" y="16" width="12" height="9" rx="2" fill="var(--plum)"/></svg></section>
