-<section aria-labelledby="object-picker-pattern"><h2 id="object-picker-pattern">Object picker</h2>
-<p>One shared React <code>ObjectPicker</code> uses the existing <code>.modal.on</code>, <code>.sheet</code>, <code>.sheeth</code>, <code>.sheetb</code>, labelled <code>.inp</code>, <code>.seg</code>, <code>.frow</code> and secondary button patterns. No page-specific picker or new stylesheet class is needed.</p>
-<p>Search by object display name; group each cursor page by source display name. At most 50 rows are mounted, with Previous objects and Next objects controls. Single selection chooses the row and closes; multiple selection uses native labelled checkboxes and an explicit Choose N objects action, preserving choices across pages. Loading, error/retry and empty search results replace the page, never its search. The modal traps focus, Escape closes, and closing restores focus to its trigger.</p>
-<p>Add override includes objects without an object default and labels those rows “no default” through the shared optional row description. It uses single selection now; the bulk bar must use this same component when it next changes. The pool page lists decisions, never the picker’s catalogue.</p></section>
